  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></math> be a complex number such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> lies on the circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and centre",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "VoxHQ",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>",
